TOOL_RESULT retrieve_history:
{"results": [], "n_results": 0}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{
 "research_concepts": [
  "Pick and Roll (PNR) effectiveness",
  "Pull-up shots (PULL_UP)",
  "Offensive counter strategies",
  "Defensive suppression",
  "Points per possession (PPP)",
  "League-wide trends"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "How to define 'PNR fail' based on available data?",
  "How to define and measure 'lift' (e.g., change in PPP or frequency)?",
  "What are the appropriate 'units' for analysis (players, teams, lineups)?",
  "How to establish a causal link between PNR failure and pull-up shot adoption/effectiveness as a counter?",
  "How to control for confounding variables in strategic analysis?"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [],
 "failed_approaches": [],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "No historical evidence was available from prior project work."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "No historical evidence was available, so nothing is established or ruled out by prior project work."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "The core concepts of PNR, PULL_UP, and points per possession are measurable with the provided data.",
  "The definition of 'PNR fail', 'counter', and 'lift' are critical operational challenges.",
  "The 'units' for analysis (players, teams, or specific lineups) need to be clearly defined to meet the '>=70% of units' criterion."
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "The precise definition of 'PNR fail' is not given, which significantly impacts how the analysis would proceed.",
  "The exact mechanism implied by 'counter' (e.g., sequential play calling, general strategic adjustment) is not specified.",
  "The baseline for calculating 'lift' (e.g., relative to overall league average, player's own average, previous PNR possessions) is not defined.",
  "The specific 'units' for analysis (players, teams, or lineups) are not specified."
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "No historical evidence was available, so it did not influence the decision."
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": 0.7,
  "blocking_constraints": []
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "no",
  "cited": [],
  "summary": "No prior project work was retrieved that addresses this specific research question."
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL",
   "text": "The definitions of 'PNR fail' and 'lift' are critical and could be arbitrarily chosen, potentially leading to findings that are artifacts of the definition rather than true strategic patterns. For example, a 'PNR fail' threshold could be set to maximize the observed 'lift'."
  },
  {
   "code": "CONFOUNDING",
   "text": "Many factors influence shot selection and effectiveness, including opponent defense, game state (score, clock), specific player matchups, and overall offensive scheme. Without careful controls, any observed 'lift' in PULL_UP PPP might be attributed to these confounders rather than PNR failure as a counter-strategy."
  },
  {
   "code": "RTM_SELECTION",
   "text": "If 'PNR fail' is defined as a particularly poor outcome (e.g., 0 points), subsequent offensive actions, including pull-up shots, might naturally regress to the mean, appearing more effective than they truly are as a strategic counter."
  },
  {
   "code": "EXPOSURE_SPARSITY",
   "text": "Depending on the definition of 'PNR fail' and the 'unit' of analysis, the number of instances where a 'counter' would be expected might be too low to achieve sufficient statistical power, especially when attempting to show an effect in '>=70% of units'."
  },
  {
   "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
   "text": "If the 'units' are defined too granularly (e.g., individual player-game segments), the sample size for detecting a median lift of 2pp might be insufficient for a statistically robust conclusion across a large percentage of units."
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": 0.3,
  "rejected": 0.3,
  "untestable": 0.2,
  "artifact": 0.1,
  "uncertain": 0.1
 },
 "decision": "proceed_with_changes",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "The primary estimand is the median 'lift' (change in Points Per Possession, PPP) of PULL_UP shots in situations following 'PNR fail' events, compared to a baseline, across defined offensive 'units'. Secondary estimands include the proportion of units exhibiting a positive 'lift' and the proportion exceeding a 2pp 'lift'.",
  "unit": "An 'offensive unit' will be defined as a specific team's offensive performance within a single NBA season (e.g., 'LAL_2024-25'). The analysis will be conducted at this team-season level.",
  "sample": "Data from NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25, and 2025-26 regular seasons and playoffs will be used. 'PNR fail' will be operationally defined as a PNR possession resulting in 0 points. A 'PULL_UP counter sequence' is defined as a PULL_UP shot attempt within 5 possessions immediately following a 'PNR fail' by the same team. The 'baseline PULL_UP PPP' for a unit will be the overall PPP of PULL_UP shots for that unit in possessions not immediately following a 'PNR fail'. The 'PULL_UP counter PPP' will be the PPP of PULL_UP shots taken within a 'PULL_UP counter sequence'.",
  "power": "With approximately 30 teams * 4 seasons = 120 team-seasons (units), and given sufficient instances of 'PNR fail' and subsequent 'PULL_UP counter sequences' per team-season, we anticipate adequate power to detect a median lift of 2pp. A minimum of 50 'PNR fail' events and 10 'PULL_UP counter sequences' per unit per season will be required for inclusion in the analysis of 'lift'. Power calculations will be refined after initial data exploration to confirm event rates.",
  "controls": "To mitigate confounding, we will compare 'PULL_UP counter PPP' against 'baseline PULL_UP PPP' for the *same unit* (team-season), controlling for game context (e.g., quarter, score differential, opponent strength via pre-game betting lines or ELO ratings) using regression adjustments if needed. Analysis will be restricted to half-court possessions to minimize transition play confounding.",
  "falsification": "A falsification test will involve analyzing the 'lift' of PULL_UP shots following *successful* PNR possessions (e.g., 2+ points). If PULL_UPs are a specific counter to PNR failure, no significant 'lift' should be observed in this falsification group. We will also test for 'lift' in other common shot types (e.g., catch-and-shoot 3s) following 'PNR fail' to ensure the effect is specific to PULL_UPs.",
  "multiplicity": "The primary hypothesis is tested at the league-wide level by assessing the median lift across all units. The '>=70% of units' criterion introduces a secondary test. No adjustments for multiple comparisons will be made across units, as each unit's analysis is considered an independent observation towards the league-wide median. However, if multiple alternative definitions of 'PNR fail' or 'PULL_UP counter sequence' are explored, appropriate multiplicity corrections (e.g., Bonferroni, FDR) will be applied.",
  "decision_rule": "The research question will be considered 'supported' if: (1) The median 'lift' (PULL_UP counter PPP - baseline PULL_UP PPP) across all included units is > 2pp, AND (2) at least 70% of included units show a positive 'lift' (PULL_UP counter PPP - baseline PULL_UP PPP > 0). Both conditions must be met with statistical significance (p < 0.05) using a Wilcoxon signed-rank test for the median lift and a binomial test for the proportion of units.",
  "data_version": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 (complete) regular season and playoffs data; NBA 2025-26 regular season (complete from 2026-04-13) and playoffs (complete from 2026-06-21) data. Derived play-type possession records and play-by-play data will be used."
 }
}

